          "filename": "Bhubaneshwar ei039.jpg",
          "caption": "Lakulisha. East Face of the tower, Parashurameshvara Temple, Bhubaneshwar\nBorn about 200 AD, Lakulisha was the chief leader\n(although perhaps not the founder) of the Pashupata sect\nof Shaivism to which this temple belonged. The seated\nholy man, who is considered by his followers to be an incarnation\nof Shiva himself, brandishes a club (his traditional attribute)\nand rosary while surrounded by four disciples arranged upon lotus blossoms. In the finely-worked decorative panel below this sculpture, an effusion of foliage is grasped by a divinity.",
